# REVIEW: A few more things you might want to add as your projects grow:
# REVIEW:   *.log              — any leftover log files
# REVIEW:   .vscode/           — your editor's local settings (unless your team
# REVIEW:                        wants to share them, in which case keep it tracked)
# REVIEW:   .idea/             — JetBrains IDE settings
# REVIEW:   /coverage          — already there, good
# REVIEW:
# REVIEW: Lesson: the goal of .gitignore is to keep YOUR-MACHINE-SPECIFIC files
# REVIEW: out of the repo. If a file would be different on someone else's
# REVIEW: computer (or contains secrets), it belongs here.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js

# testing
/coverage

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
